## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical lightweight baseline building for text routing under strict latency constraints, in a data-scarce regime with model calibration requirements. Also covers drift monitoring and retraining cadence.

## Key Concepts
- Lightweight text representation with a fixed 30-feature vector
- SGD-based multiclass logistic regression or tiny decision tree for efficiency
- Calibration via temperature scaling
- Drift detection using rolling holdout validation
- Deployment latency and monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Training loop outline for SGD multiclass LR
const model = new SGDLogisticRegression({
  learningRate: 0.01,
  epochs: 100,
  batchSize: 32
});
model.fit(XTrain, yTrain);
// Temperature scaling for calibration
const temp = calibrateTemperature(model, XVal, yVal);
// Inference
const predict = (features) => {
  const start = performance.now();
  const probs = model.predictProb(features, temp);
  const latency = performance.now() - start;
  return { probs, latency };
};
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a practical, beginner-friendly ML pipeline for churn with real-world constraints: leakage prevention, encoding choices, and model comparisons that balance performance and interpretability.

## Key Concepts

- Data leakage prevention via time-based or grouped splits
- Handling class imbalance in binary targets
- Baseline vs tree-based models and interpretability
- Evaluation metrics: AUROC andPR-AUC, plus feature importance tools like SHAP

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo baseline pipeline (illustrative only)
function trainBaseline(data){
  const X = oneHotEncode(data.features);
  const {train, test} = timeSplit(X, data.labels);
  const model = trainLR(train.features, train.labels, {C:1.0});
  const preds = model.predict(test.features);
  return evaluate(test.labels, preds);
}
```

